  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Designing the Dashboard**\n\nI\'m starting to visualize the structure of the trading dashboard. Currently, I\'m focusing on the header and top bar elements. I\'m thinking of incorporating a brand title, like \"ATR QUANT BOT\" or \"VOLATILITY TRADER.\" An active coin selector, featuring options like BTC/USDT, ETH/USDT, etc., seems essential for a user-friendly interface.\n\n\n**Visualizing Trading Data**\n\nI\'ve been drilling down into the specific data visualizations for the dashboard\'s chart. I\'m focusing on the Volatility ATR Chart, imagining upper and lower bands, a baseline, and a dynamic stop-loss line. I\'m visualizing a candlestick or price line history, shaded ATR channel, and a real-time price indicator with a pulsing dot. It\'s becoming clearer how I can incorporate buy/sell execution markers directly on the chart to give the user a clear picture.\n\n\n**Defining Dashboard Interaction**\n\nI\'m now focusing on user interactions and trading controls. I envision buy/sell markers directly on the chart, complete with interactive crosshair data on price, ATR, and timestamps. I\'ve designed interactive timeframe switchers. The trading position and metric stats cards will display current position, PnL, win rate, and balance, which should be very useful. I\'m imagining parameter sliders and config for ATR multiplier, order size, stop loss, tick frequency, and volatility noise. Finally, there will be a real-time trading log console.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 43
      nanos: 198216128
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
